{"id":"u-1c73ef00-8ee5-4250-9058-9f96fd0504e5","src":"community","title":"Jax PPL","author":"Jax S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/yLgfYo-untitled-program","desc":"Myo-Rep Match (Advance progression)\nStart with regular sets; we’ll introduce myo-rep matching once you’re comfortable with the program and recovering well.\nComplete your first set normally as close to 1 RIR (Rep in Reserve) as possible. On later sets, use the same weight and match the first set’s total reps, taking short 10–15-second breaks as needed to finish set. Rest normally between full sets, and maintain good form throughout.\n\nRest Days\nFollow three training days with one rest day: Pull → Push → Legs → Rest, then repeat with the next three workouts. This spacing helps manage fatigue, especially in the lower back. Workout numbers show the order, not fixed weekdays\n\nExercise Substitutes\nEach workout has a specific focus, but exercises can be swapped when equipment is occupied or time is limited. Choose a similar movement targeting the same muscles; for example, a machine chest press in place of a dumbbell chest press. Ask me if you’re unsure about a substitution\n\nIncreasing Weight\nIncrease weight when you can complete the top of the rep range on every regular set with controlled form and 1–2 good reps still available. For example, 3 × 8–12 means reaching 12 reps on all three sets before increasing.\n\nUpper body barbell compounds: Add 5 lb total—2.5 lb per side.\n- Lower-body barbell compounds: Add 10 lb total—5 lb per side.\n- Dumbbells, machines, and isolation exercises: Use the smallest practical increase.\n\nAfter Increasing\nit’s normal to return to the lower end of the rep range. If you cannot reach it with good form, use a smaller increase or stay at your previous weight. We’ll review myo-rep match progression separately.\n\nRecovery and Deloads\nLet me know if fatigue or soreness keeps carrying into your next workout, or your performance starts dropping across several sessions. We’ll adjust the workload and, when needed, schedule a deload...a short period of lighter training...to help you recover and keep progressing","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-09T01:20:08.006Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push (Bench)","Pull (Deadlift)","Legs (Squat)","Push (Shoulders)","Pull (Back)","Legs (Ham/Glutes)"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pec Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo